"{\"url\":\"https://www.microcision.com/about-1\",\"title\":\"QUALITY ASSURANCE INSPECTOR | Microcision\",\"desc\":null,\"og\":null,\"robots\":null,\"imgs\":[\"Microcision logo.png | 31e942_ef154a865afe4fa79723417987ebbaeb~mv2.png\"],\"form\":[],\"iframes\":[],\"sha256\":\"8ec02e9532f51141dfde1df9d3f63fa0940881390ec7578beda8fc6219dcd04d\",\"text\":\"Skip to Main Content\\n\\nHOME\\n\\nSERVICES\\n\\nABOUT\\n\\nEXPANSION\\n\\nCAREERS\\n\\nCONTACT\\n\\nQuality Assurance Inspector\\n\\n\\u00a0\\n\\nPrimary duties and responsibilities include:\\n\\n\\u00a0\\n\\nPerform first piece, in process, and final inspection of machined parts.\\n\\nAssist machine programmers and set-up personnel to optimize both milling and screw machine set-up time and machine utilization.\\n\\nCompletion of internal and customer required quality documentation.\\n\\n\\nPreferred candidates would be able to meet to meet the following requirements:\\n\\n\\u00a0\\n\\n(3) years minimum inspection experience preferably with machined parts.\\n\\nCMM experience a plus.\\n\\nOptical Measuring device experience (OGP, Keyence, Microvue, Nikon or similar).\\n\\nBackground in reading blueprints - Geometric Dimensioning & Tolerancing,\\n\\nCapability to use all standard measuring tools such as optical comparators calipers, micrometers, go/no-go and thread gauges, surface plate instruments.\\n\\nAble to use a computer and have a working knowledge of Microsoft Office. (Outlook / Excel / Word).\\n\\nAbility to multi-task and be flexible in a fast-paced manufacturing environment.\\n\\nBasic understanding of a Quality Management Systems\\n\\n\\nJob Type: Full-time\\n\\n\\nPay: $17.00 - $21.00 per hour\\n\\u00a0\\n\\n\\u00a9 2022\\u00a0by Microcision LLC\"}"
